From 573a3cf97091c4ceb0d84af054ce2cc9fd14227d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Dec 2021 09:35:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 092/165] KVM: TDX: Handle EXCEPTION_NMI and EXTERNAL_INTERRUPT

Handle EXCEPTION_NMI and EXTERNAL_INTERRUPT exits for TDX.

Ignore NMIs and machine checks for EXCEPTION_NMI exit because they are
already handled elsewhere.
- NMIs are handled by tdx_handle_exit(), prior to leaving the safety of
  noinstr.
- Machine check occurs during TDX non-root operation is handled by
  vmx_handle_exception_irqoff() and machine check occurs during entry is
  handled by tdx_handle_exit().

For other exceptions, because guest TD state is protected, exceptions in
guest TDs can't be intercepted.  TDX VMM isn't supposed to handle these
exceptions.  If unexpected exception occurs, exit to userspace with
KVM_EXIT_EXCEPTION.

For external interrupt, increase the statistics, same to the VMX case.

